 ### Reading resources and cards
 
 Small cubes are green (Food & Life Support), white (Culture) and brown (Industry). Large cubes are black (Information), blue (Biotechnology) and yellow (Power). Octagons are Ultratech. Gray cubes are Unity wild resources, available in both sizes. Color, size and shape matter; a wild input/output never substitutes across sizes.
 
-Ordinary victory points stay face down behind your screen and cannot be traded. Resources and cards remain visible; only points and ships being hidden for bidding go behind screens. Ship designs do not change their rules. Nominal trade values are guidance: roughly one point = one octagon = two large cubes = three small cubes; a ship is roughly one small cube. Converter values printed below arrows are measured in small cubes and help negotiate; they do not replace actual input costs.
